  "topic_en": "Euler tabulates, for small prime values of a (2 through 29), the numbers of the form 4n+1 split into the class T (of the form (2q+1)^2 - 4ai) and the excluded class Θ, listing the first period below 4a and following periods obtained by adding 4a.",
  "transcription": "— 284 —\n\n$1, 5, 9, 13, 17, 21, 25, 29, 33,$ etc.\npro quouis casu numeri $a$ siue ad ordinem terminorum $T = (2q+1)^2 - 4ai$, siue ad ordinem excluſorum $\\Theta$ referantur, operae pretium erit, ambos iſtos ordines, pro minoribus ſaltem ipſius $a$ valoribus, qui quidem ſint primi, exhibere; atque vtile erit, non ſolum primam periodum horum numerorum ipſo $4a$ minorum, ſed etiam ſequentes periodos, addendo continuo $4a$, ob oculos exponere:\n\n1°. Sit $a = 2$; erit $4a = 8$.\n$T = 1 | 9 | 17 | 25 | 33 |$\n$\\Theta = 5 | 13 | 21 | 29 | 37 |$ etc.\n\n2°. Sit $a = 3$; erit $4a = 12$.\n$T = 1 | 13 | 25 | 37 | 49 | 61 |$\n$\\Theta = 5 | 17 | 29 | 41 | 53 | 65 |$ etc.\nQuia hic $a$ erat $3$, quadrata per $3$ diuiſibilia excludi debebant:\n\n3°. Sit $a = 5$; erit $4a = 20$.\n$T = 1, 9 | 21, 29 | 41, 49 | 61, 69 | 81, 89 |$ etc.\n$\\Theta = 13, 17 | 33, 37 | 53, 57 | 73, 77 | 93, 97 |$\nHic ſcilicet ex ordine $\\Theta$ excluſimus numerum $5$, vtpote ipſi $a$ aequalem.\n\n4°. Sit $a = 7$; erit $4a = 28$.\n$T = 1, 9, 25 | 29, 37, 53 | 57, 65, 81 |$\n$\\Theta = 5[?], 13, 17 | 33, 41, 45 | 61, 69, 73 |$ etc.\nHic in ordine $\\Theta$ omiſimus numerum $21$, vtpote per $a = 7$ diuiſibilem.\n\n5°.\n\n— 285 —\n\n5°. Sit $a = 11$; $4a = 44$.\n$T = 1, 5, 9, 25, 37 | 45, 49, 53, 69, 81 |$ etc.\n$\\Theta = 13, 17, 21, 29, 41 | 57, 61, 65, 73, 85 |$\n$89, 93, 97, 113, 125$\n$101, 105, 109, 117, 129 |$ etc.\n\n6°. Sit $a = 13$; $4a = 52$.\n$T = 1, 9, 17, 25, 29, 49, 53, 61, 69, 77, 81, 101,$ etc.\n$\\Theta = 5, 21, 33, 37, 41, 45, 57, 73, 85, 89, 93, 97,$ etc.\n\n7°. Sit $a = 17$; $4a = 68$.\n$T = 1, 9, 13, 21, 25, 33, 49, 53,$ etc.\n$\\Theta = 5, 29, 37, 41, 45, 57, 61, 65,$ etc.\n\n8°. Sit $r = 19$; $4a = 76$.\n$T = 1, 5, 9, 17, 25, 45, 49, 61, 73, 77, 81, 85, 93,$\n$101, 121, 125, 137, 149,$ etc.\n$\\Theta = 13, 21, 29, 33, 37, 41, 53, 65, 69, 89, 97, 105,$\n$109, 113, 117, 129, 141, 145,$ etc.\n\n9°. Sit $a = 23$; $4a = 92$.\n$T = 1, 9, 13, 25, 29, 41, 49, 73, 77, 81, 85,$ etc.\n$\\Theta = 5, 17, 21, 33, 37, 45, 53, 57, 61, 65, 89,$ etc.\n\n10°. Sit $a = 29$; $4a = 116$.\n$T = 1, 5, 9, 13, 25, 33, 45, 49, 53, 57, 65, 81, 93,$\n$109,$ etc.\n$\\Theta = 17, 21, 37, 41, 61, 69, 73, 77, 85, 89, 97, 105,$\n$105, 113,$ etc.\n\nN n 3 \\qquad Scho-",
